{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118345","id":3508731450,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7RIv46","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118345","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118345.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118345.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118345","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118345/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118345/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118345/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/67802d72826342c471113a9a8b5fe97ae4535cc1","number":118345,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix GLTFPhysicsShape import/export for OMI_physics_shape capsules and cylinders","user":{"login":"k1r4n8","id":136159557,"node_id":"U_kgDOCB2hRQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/136159557?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/k1r4n8","html_url":"https://github.com/k1r4n8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k1r4n8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k1r4n8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k1r4n8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k1r4n8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k1r4n8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k1r4n8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k1r4n8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k1r4n8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k1r4n8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Importing a glTF file containing a capsule/cylinder compliant with the OMI_physics_shape spec currently ignores the `radiusTop`/`radiusBottom` fields. Additionally the spec defines `height` to be the mid-height for capsules and total height for cylinders, but both are currently interpreted as total height.\r\nThe `GLTFPhysicsShape` documentation states that both OMI_physics_shape and OMI_collider are supported and that its `to_dictionary()` method serializes in the format defined by OMI_physics_shape.\r\n\r\nThis change makes capsule and cylinder imports read `radiusTop` and `radiusBottom` (falling back to `radius`) and interpret `height` depending on the shape type. Since Godot does not have tapered capsules/cylinders the importer emits a warning when `radiusTop` and `radiusBottom` differ and uses their average as an approximation.\r\nOMI_collider imports are still working like before. To avoid changing method signatures or adding new helpers I used an `extension` field in the dictionary to distinguish between OMI_physics_shape and OMI_collider handling.\r\nThe `to_dictionary()` method now sets `radiusTop`/`radiusBottom` (identical) and `height` values that are compliant with OMI_physics_shape.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310502,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA1MDI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:import","name":"topic:import","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release."